### Workflow API Test Suite
### Based on Diagrid Catalyst Workflow Quickstart
### https://docs.diagrid.io/catalyst/quickstart/workflow

### Health Check
GET http://localhost:5001/

###

### Start Workflow
// @name startWorkflow
POST http://localhost:5001/workflow/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Car",
  "quantity": 2
}

###

### Get Workflow Status
### Uses the workflow ID from the previous start request
@instanceId={{startWorkflow.response.body.instanceId}}
GET http://localhost:5001/workflow/status/{{instanceId}}

###

### Terminate Workflow
### Uses the workflow ID from the previous start request
@instanceId={{startWorkflow.response.body.instanceId}}
POST http://localhost:5001/workflow/terminate/{{instanceId}}

###

### Crash Recovery: run under an ID you own
# Blocks for ~30s while the slow activity commits, up to a 120s wait budget. Kill
# the app during that window with the request below. Restarting the app is what
# recovers the run; send this exact request again only to read back its answer,
# because the crash killed the connection that was waiting for one. Use an id you
# have not used before: an id that already names a finished run just attaches to it
# and answers instantly, with no crash to see.
POST http://localhost:5001/crash/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "trip-42",
  "reference": "ABC123"
}

###

### Crash Recovery: kill the app
# Send this while the run above is still in flight. The process dies before it can
# reply, so this request reports a connection reset rather than a status code.
POST http://localhost:5001/crash/kill

###
